Here's a simple HTML website that meets your requirements. It uses a minimal, clean design and includes a button that triggers a random joke from a list of 4 jokes.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Random Joke Generator</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 16px;
            background-color: #4a90e2;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #357ab8;
        }
        #joke-container {
            margin-top: 20px;
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.4;
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Random Joke</h1>
    <button id="showJoke">Show Joke</button>
    <div id="joke-container">
        <!-- Joke will be inserted here -->
    </div>

    <script>
        // List of 4 jokes (as plain strings)
        const jokes = [
            "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
            "I told my wife she was drawing her eyebrows too high. She looked surprised.",
            "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
            "What do you call a fake noodle? An impasta."
        ];

        // Get the button and container element
        const button = document.getElementById('showJoke');
        const jokeContainer = document.getElementById('joke-container');

        // Function to show a random joke
        function showRandomJoke() {
            // Pick a random index from the jokes array
            const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
            // Get the selected joke
            const joke = jokes[randomIndex];
            // Update the container with the joke
            jokeContainer.textContent = joke;
        }

        // Attach click event to the button
        button.addEventListener('click', showRandomJoke);
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works:
- The page displays a simple heading ("Random Joke"), a button labeled "Show Joke", and a placeholder where the joke will appear.
- When you click the button, the script picks one random joke from the `jokes` array (which contains exactly 4 jokes).
- The selected joke is displayed in the `#joke-container` div.
- The design is clean, responsive for most screens, and uses basic CSS for readability.
- No external libraries or complex code—just plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

### To use:
1. Copy the entire code above.
2. Save it as `index.html` (or any name you like) in a folder.
3. Open the file in any web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari, etc.).
4. Click the "Show Joke" button—each click will show a different random joke from the 4 listed.

